@startuml System Architecture

' ============================================================================
' System Architecture Diagram
' ============================================================================
' This diagram shows the high-level architecture of the A/B Testing API.
'
' Key components:
' - Clients: Web apps, mobile apps, CLI tools connect via HTTPS
' - Authentication: Bearer token validation for all protected endpoints
' - API Routers: Handle /experiments, /events, /flags endpoints
' - Caching: In-memory cache reduces database load
' - Repository Layer: Abstracts database access (Repository Pattern)
' - PostgreSQL: Persistent storage for all data
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

title A/B Testing API - System Architecture (Repository Pattern)

' ===== Clients =====
actor "Web App" as Web
actor "Mobile App" as Mobile
actor "CLI/Scripts" as CLI

' ===== API Layer =====
rectangle "Docker Container" as Docker #LightBlue {

    rectangle "FastAPI Application" as API #LightGreen {

        rectangle "Authentication" as AuthLayer #LightYellow {
            [Bearer Token\nValidation] as Auth
        }

        rectangle "API Routers" as Endpoints #LightCyan {
            [/experiments] as Exp
            [/events] as Event
            [/flags] as Flags
        }

        rectangle "Caching" as CacheLayer #LightPink {
            [In-Memory Cache\n(TTL: 1-5 min)] as Cache
        }

        rectangle "Repository Layer" as RepoLayer #Wheat {
            [ExperimentRepository] as ExpRepo
            [EventRepository] as EventRepo
            [FeatureFlagRepository] as FlagRepo
        }

        rectangle "Repository Implementations" as RepoImpl #LightGray {
            [SQLAlchemy\nImplementations] as SQLAImpl
        }
    }

    database "PostgreSQL" as DB #WhiteSmoke {
        [experiments]
        [variants]
        [assignments]
        [events]
        [feature_flags]
    }
}

' ===== Connections =====
Web --> Auth : HTTPS
Mobile --> Auth : HTTPS
CLI --> Auth : HTTPS

Auth --> Exp
Auth --> Event
Auth --> Flags

Exp --> Cache : read/write
Flags --> Cache : read/write

Exp --> ExpRepo : interface
Event --> EventRepo : interface
Flags --> FlagRepo : interface

ExpRepo --> SQLAImpl
EventRepo --> SQLAImpl
FlagRepo --> SQLAImpl

SQLAImpl --> DB

' ===== Notes =====
note bottom of Docker
  **Running Command:**
  docker-compose up

  **Port:** 8000
  **Docs:** /docs
end note

note right of RepoLayer
  **Abstraction Layer:**
  - Hides DB implementation
  - Enables easy testing
  - Supports DB switching
end note

note right of Cache
  **Cached Data:**
  - User assignments
  - Flag evaluations

  **Purpose:**
  Reduce DB queries
  for frequent calls
end note

@enduml
